Research:
    There exists multiple parking platforms or apps that include ParkMobile, SpotHero, ParkWhiz, and BestParking.
    Many of these apps and platforms provide parking availability and convienent accessiblity towards paying the fees.
    To be different, I am including parking predictibility, parking recommendations, violation prevention, and accessibility-based parking that uses an AI to help manage and guide the usersto their desired parking needs.

Vision & Scope:
    $oftware Corp is a software development studio that works with companies and organizations to aid in needs of everyday struggles. This project was acquired through the demand for a centralized and efficient approach to parking management. The Smart Parking Platform handles the issues that everyday parking has like congestion, frustration, and the lack of productivity in finding spaces. The project will examine exisiting parking solutions and find opportunities to improve user experience and needs with real-time information, improved parking management and payment, and AI aided recommendation.
    The software will provide:
        User registration and authentication
        Real-time parking space availability
        Interactive map displaying available parking locations
        Parking reservation capability
        Digital payment processing
        Reservation history and receipts
        Administrative dashboard for parking operators
        Occupancy reporting and analytics
        Notifications and alerts for users
        Integration with external mapping/navigation services


Software Requirements Specification (SRS):
    Project: Parking$MART
    Version 1.0
    Date: 09.09.26
    
    1. Introduction
    1.1 Purpose
        Requirements for Parking$MART is to allow users to efficiently find available parking spaces through interactice maps with real-time parking availability, provides notifications and reservations, and accessible digital payments. Parking operators will have a dashboard to manage the parking garages/spaces, monitor occupancy, and parking analytics. The project will help users spend less time in searching for parking and allow operators to have improve management of parking facilities.
    1.2 Scope
        Parking$MART will be available on mobile and web applications that users to locate available parking spaces, make parking reservations, receive notifications on parking accessibility, and complete digital payments on the app. For parking operators, it will allow them to manage and administer parking spaces and occupancy, review reservations, and generate reports and analytics. Some things that are out of scope for the project will be parking enforcement, any vehicle tracking, automated vehicle parking, or any physical structures that within parking garages/spaces like gates, cameras, sensors, etc.

    2. Overall Description
        - Users: 
            Drivers/Vehicle Owners looking for parking spaces
            Parking Operators/Administrators
            Third-Party payments services
        - System Environment: Web-based/Mobile application
        - Constraints:
            Development time has to be within 4 months
            run on cloud-based software to allow web/mobile based application
            hardware must be high-end to handle sensors and other equipment for parking
            for parking operators must need code/biometric authentication to access parking managment/admin
            high-level of security to secure account, payment, and reservation information
            Third-Party dependencies like mapping, payment, and other services.

    3. Functional Requirements
       FR1: User Registration
        Program shall allow new users to create an account using required information to register
       FR2: User Authentication
        Program shall allow users to log in and out of their accounts
       FR3: Real-Time Parking Availability
        Program shall show users current availability of parking garages/spaces
       FR4: Interactive Parking Map
        Software shall show users an interactive map to show parking spots
       FR5: Parking Search
        Software shall allow users to find any parking based on their needs
       FR6: Parking Reservation
        Program shall allow users to reserve a parking spot
       FR7: Digital Payment
        Program shall allow users to pay digitally for parking reservations
       FR8: Reservation History
        Program shall contain a history of user reservations
       FR9: Reservation Receipt
        Program shall give users a receipt after a payment
       FR10: Notifications/Alerts
        Program shall alert users of important parking events
       FR11: Parking Admin Dashboard
        Program shall give authorized parking personnel a dashboard of analytics and information regarding parking garages/spaces
       FR12: Parking Management
        Program shall allow authorized parking operators to manage parking spaces
       FR13: Role-Based Access Control
        Software shall limit user functions based on user role
       FR14: Navigation/Mapping integration
        Software shall integrate with a mapping service
       FR15: Simultaneous Reservation Prevention
        Software shall prevent mutliple users from reserving the same parking space at overlapping times
       FR16: User Double Booking
        Software shall prevent double-booking from a user  
    
    4. Non-Functional Requirements
        NFR1: Program shall support at least 1 million concurrent users
        NFR2: Program shall process user registration within 3 seconds
        NFR3: Program shall process user reservation within 10 seconds
        NFR4: Program shall update parking availability within 10 seconds after receiving registration/occupancy data
        NFR5: Program shall provide 99.99% uptime
        NFR6: Program shall process payment methods comepltely and securely within 3 seconds


    5. Use Case Examples
        USC-1:
            Title: Registering for an account
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: User does not have an account for the Software
            Steps:
                1. User taps/selects "Register"
                2. Program displays reigstration form
                3. User inputs required information
                4. User clicks submit
                5. Program validates information
                6. Program creates account
                7. Program confirms successful registration
            Postcondition: New user account is created
        USC-2:
            Title: Logging into Program
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: user has an existing account, but not logged in
            Steps:
                1.User enters their email and password
                2. Program validates information
                3. Program authenticates user
                4. Program displays users home page
            Postcondition: User is granted access to the program
        USC-3:
            Title: Parking Search
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: User has access to program and is looking for a parking spot given destination/search location
            Steps:
                1. User enters information on destination (zip code, address, etc.)
                2. Program searches available
            Postcondition: Program shows available parking spaces that match the user's search
        USC-4:
            Title: Looking for Real-time availabilty for parking
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: Parking spaces are in the program and occupancy information is available
            Steps:
            Postcondition: User is shown available and occupied spaces on an interactive map live
        USC-5:
            Title: Viewing interactive map 
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: User has access to program and live locations are available in the program
            Steps:
            Postcondition: User is shown parking spaces/garages on an interactive map
        USC-6:
            Title: View Parking details/data
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: Parking space exists and user selects it
            Steps:
            Postcondition: Information related to selected parking space is displayed
        USC-7:
            Title: Reserving Parking Space
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: User is logged into program, parking space is available, Parking period is available
            Steps:
            Postcondition: Parking space is reserved and created during user's selected period
        USC-8:
            Title: User makes digital payment
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: User has a valid and available payment method, User has made a valid reservation
            Steps:
            Postcondition: Payment is processed and confirms reservation, transaction is successful
        USC-9:
            Title: Viewing Reservation History
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: User has at least one reservation confirmed/processed
            Steps:
            Postcondition: User's current and previous reservations are shown
        USC-10:
            Title: View Receipt
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: User has a completed reservation with a successful payment
            Steps:
            Postcondition: User is shown receipt information with related payment
        USC-11:
            Title: Receiving notifications and alerts
            Actor: User/Driver/Parking Admin
            Precondition: User is logged into their respective accounts and notifcations are enabled, a related event occurs
            Steps:
            Postcondition: Related/relevant notification is shown/sent to the user 
        USC-12:
            Title: Managing Parking spaces
            Actor: Parking Admin
            Precondition: Admin is authenticated and has admin privileges
            Steps:
            Postcondition: Selected parking spaces can be updated, added, or removed
        USC-13:
            Title: Managing Reservations
            Actor: Parking Admin
            Precondition: Admin is authenticated and has admin privileges, reservations are active
            Steps:
            Postcondition: Reservations are updated, denied, or viewed by the Admin
        USC-14:
            Title: Looking at occupancy analytics/reports
            Actor: Parking Admin
            Precondition: Admin is authenticated and has admin privileges, occupancy data is in the program
            Steps:
            Postcondition: Occupancy-related analytics and reports are shown to the admin
        USC-15:
            Title: Navigation directions to selected parking spot
            Actor: User/Driver
            Precondition: User selects parking garage/spot, external mapping service is up
            Steps:
            Postcondition: User receives directions towards their selected parking garage/spot




